ls they  have limited choices and come with a  blueprint of their own and as a result  the user doesn't have much control so  javascript being an interpreted language  where code is executed line by line  makes all these tools very efficient  mainly because converting the code into  an intermediate code would require a  runtime environment and would definitely  encounter a delay now these are avoided  and as a result these tools are fast  moving on react is used to develop  mobile and web applications and angular  is used for single page applications and  you can also develop hybrid applications  using the stack mainly because it's  purely based on css html javascript and  jquery single page applications as the  name suggests are built using single  page now the entire page is broken down  into several components wherein each  component performs a specific task say  for example one component handles the  login the other one would display icons  and images and so on all these bits or  components are then put together to form  a single page application and moving on  react was developed and maintained by  facebook while angular was built by  google and view was developed by evan  unx google employee now react represents  the view part of the mvc framework and  angular is a full-fledged mvc framework  in itself and view on the other hand is  focused on view and the model layer of  the mvc framework now what exactly is  the mvc framework now mvc framework is  an object-oriented design principle that  mandates the separation of control  meaning one thing can only do one thing  so the model deals with the entity  classes the data and the business logic  while view deals with the representation  and the ui logic of the application and  the controller drives the functionality  of the two any changes can be easily  factored and isolated and as a result  testing becomes a whole lot easier  moving on now let's look at the use  cases from the business perspective in  terms of react we have top websites like  facebook instagram netflix that use  react on the other hand we have angular  that is used by nike hbo forbes sony and  vue is commonly used by alibaba.com  grammarly 9gag and adobe moving on we  have performance now performance is a  very crucial feature now the moment you  build an html view and render it into  the browser this view to the user is  basically just html tags however if you  look at the internal working the code is  actually converted into a balanced tree  structure this b3 algorithm is extremely  fast so when the user makes any changes  to the ui the changes are reflected  immediately this is facilitated by the  b3 algorithm so as a result the  performance is improved so how does  react make use of this tool it uses a  virtual dom dom is an api developed by  w3c it stands for document object model  and defines how the document is accessed  and manipulated this dom parser converts  the html code into an inverse balance  tree structure so react uses the virtual  dom while angular uses the real dom and  vue uses the virtual dom again now the  virtual dom looks at the differences  between the current and the previous  html pages and only changes the parts  that need to be updated angular on the  other hand updates the entire tree  structure regardless of any changes made  or not and view again only updates the  ones that have changed since there is no  time spent on making unnecessary changes  to the entire tree react is extremely  fast on the other hand real dom updation  is time consuming risky and error-prone  vue also ensures faster and bug free  performance now let's talk about data  binding the core reason why we would use  single page applications now consider a  scenario where you log into an  e-commerce website as say user one then  you should be able to see the items in  your shopping cart while user 2 would be  seeing different items in their shopping  carts and so on so identifying the user  and retrieving data corresponding to  that specific user is facilitated using  the help of data binding data binding is  a process that allows an internet user  to manipulate web page elements using a  web browser now it is used in  interactive components such as  calculators tutorials games etc now  react supports one way data binding  meaning you can take the data from the  view and push it to the model or vice  versa angular on the other hand uses a  two-way data binding while view also  uses a similar two-way data binding in  react every time the model state updates  the view changes accordingly however the  reverse is not true in case of angular  any changes made to the view are  immediately reflected in the model part  of the architecture view follows the  same principle now this hugely  influences the performance due to  one-way data binding react is modular  and fast improving the performance  angular's two-way data binding adversely  affects the performance and view on the  other hand performs according to the  input type moving on to scripting  languages react combines ui templates  and javascript logic resulting in a new  language called jsx so react only  requires the knowledge of javascript  angular uses templates again in html you  can also inject javascript code into  html using a clever implementation in  angular called directives so you can  create a class and then inject it into  html angular also does something better  you can also write code for an angular  application using a newer language  developed by microsoft called typescript  it is a compiled language and is very  similar to java and c-sharp in terms of  syntax now vue again uses html based  template it uses html5 throughout for  the ui and the combination of javascript  for business logic all view templates  are valid html and can be passed by html  parsers let's move on to testing now  jest is a framework or an api that is  developed by facebook and is used to run  tests on react applications to ensure  that they are bug free now it is  embedded typically in every react  library and requires zero configuration  now angular on the other hand uses the  jasmine framework now this framework  allows various functionalities to write  different kinds of test cases this also  ensures that the application is error  free the view cli or the command line  interpreter has built-in options for  unit testing with the help of jest or  mocha now vue typically has single file  components and hence these components  can be tested in isolation this makes it  modular and extremely fast now let's  talk about community support since all  these tools are open source they have a  large developer community there are a  few popular github repositories for  react such as react.js 101 react.js.org  and so on you can raise queries solve a  few and connect with the larger  community that's working on react here  are a few repositories for angular view  also has a few popular repositories you  can commit download third party plugins  and also explore these stacks even  deeper all of them surely have a very  happening community at the time of  writing there were about 1 million  repositories 5 million comments and 1  million issues with respect to react  here are the figures for angular and  here are the figures for view according  to npm stat over the past two years  there have been approximately 360  million react.js downloads there have  been around 38 million downloads for  angular and around 63 million downloads  for view now let's look at the future  scope learning a new technology always  comes with questions like what's in it  for me what's its growth potential how  far will it take me in my career and so  on so let's go ahead and see the growth  rate of react angular and vue according  to google trends over the past 12 months  react has been on a way faster upward  trajectory than angular and vue which  have considerably lost their momentum  now this indicates that react is growing  faster than the other two with respect  to popularity industry adoption and  community support in this video i  present to you some commonly asked  angular interview questions  now let's begin  i've classified the questions into two  sections  one is the beginner level questions and  one is the advanced level questions  so now let's begin with beginner level  questions  starting with the most basic what  exactly is angular  now angular is an open source javascript  front-end framework which is completely  written in typescript  this framework brings a structure and  consistency to web applications and  provides excellent scalability and  maintainability  now it's primarily aimed to develop  single page applications and is  maintained by google  it uses html syntax to express your  application's components clearly it is  designed for web desktop and mobile  platforms  next up is what exactly is typescript  now typescript is a superset of  javascript that offers excellent  consistency  it is highly recommended as it provides  some syntactic sugar and makes the code  base more comfortable to understand and  maintain  ultimately typescript code compiles down  to javascript that can run efficiently  in any environment now typically  typescript is installed as an npm  package and thus can be installed with  the following command that is npm  install hyphen g typescript  moving on to our third question  what exactly is data binding and which  type of data binding does angular deploy  now data binding is a phenomenon that  allows any internet user to manipulate  web page elements  now it generally uses dynamic html and  does not require any complex scripting  or programming  we use data binding in pages that  contain interactive components such as  forms calculators  tutorials and games  data binding makes incremental display  of a web page more convenient  when it comes to angular it uses the  two-way data binding  any changes made to the user interface  are reflected in the corresponding model  state  conversely any changes in the model  state are reflected in the ui state  this allows the framework to connect the  dom to the model data via the controller  next question what are single page  applications  single page applications are web  applications that load just once with  new features just being mere additions  to the user interface  it does not load new html pages to  display the content  instead is generated dynamically  this is made possible through  javascript's ability to manipulate the  dom elements on the existing page itself  an spa approach is faster thus providing  a seamless user experience  differentiate between angular and  angularjs  now here's a simple table for you  so here are the features that we're  going to differentiate  the 2 on the basis of  first is language angularjs uses  javascript while angular uses typescript  when it comes to architecture angularjs  supports the model view controller  design while angular uses components and  directives angularjs is not supported by  mobile browsers  while angular supports all mobile  browsers  angularjs does not support dependency  injection while angular does  when it comes to routing at route  provider is used to provide routing  information in the case of angularjs and  in case of angular at route  configuration is used to define routing  information  when it comes to management angularjs is  difficult to manage with an increase in  source code size  while angular is better structured easy  to create and can manage bigger  applications  next up what are decorators in angular  decorators are a design pattern or  functions that define how angular  features work  now they are used to make prior  modifications to a class service or  filter  angular supports four types of  decorators namely class decorators  property decorators method decorators  and parameter decorators  next question mention some advantages of  angular first up is custom components  now angular enables users to build their  own components that can pack  functionality along with rendering logic  into reusable pieces  this is achieved with the help of these  components  data binding as discussed earlier  angular enables users to effortlessly  move data from javascript code to the  view and react to users events without  having to write any code manually  angular supports dependency injection  which enables users to write modular  services and inject them wherever they  need it  when it comes to testing tests are first  class tools and angular has been built  from ground up with testability in mind  you will have the ability to test every  part of your application and that is  highly recommended  next up is comprehensive angular is a  full-fledged framework and provides  out-of-the-box solutions for server  communication routing with your  application and more  lastly angular is cross-platform and  compatible with multiple browsers an  angular application can typically run on  all browsers be it chrome firefox safari  and operating systems like windows mac  os and linux  what's new with angular 10 first up is  that older versions of typescript are  not supported  previous versions of angular supported  typescript 3.6 3.7 and even 3.8 but with  angular 10 typescript bumped to  typescript 3.9  warnings about common js imports now  logging of unknown property bindings or  element names in templates is increased  to the error level which was previously  a warning  angular now supports an optional strict  setting which offers a stricter project  setup when you create a new workspace  there's an addition of ngcc features  with the program based entry point  finder there are common compiler updates  and updated url routing  angular 10 has several deprecated apis  that were previously redundant  with angular 10 version there have been  a number of bug fixes important ones  being the compiler avoiding undefined  expressions and the core avoiding a  migration error  new default browser configuration  browser configuration for new projects  has been upgraded to outdo older and  less used browsers  next up is core all the warnings will be  now logged in as errors  next update is converting pre-iv code  now all the pre-iv dependencies from npm  should be transformed to iv dependencies  which is supposed to take place as a  precursor to running ngtsc at the  application  and lastly we have service workers for  the service worker a fix has been put in  for a situation in which there was a  chance that the service worker would not  register when there is a long running  task or a recurring timeout  next up  is what are templates in angular  now angular templates are written with  html that contains angular specific  elements and attributes  now in combination with  model and controllers information  these templates can be rendered to  provide a dynamic view to the user now  templates are a very predominant feature  of angular that describe how information  can be displayed in the view  next question is what are annotations in  angular  now these annotations are used to create  an annotation array  they are basically the metadata set on  the class that is used to reflect the  metadata library  what are directives in angular  directives are attributes that allow the  user to write new html syntax specific  to their applications  now these execute whenever the angular  compiler finds them in the dom  now again angular supports three  different types of directives there are  component directives attribute  directives and structural directives  next up what is aot compilation and what  are some of its advantages  now aots that stands for ahead of time  compiler basically converts the angular  html and typescript into javascript code  during the build phase  that is before the browser downloads and  runs the code  so basically all the html and typescript  code is converted to javascript during  the build phase which means no  additional time is spent on converting  it into javascript later during the run  phase right so when it comes to  advantages  of course there's faster rendering  there are fewer asynchronous requests  it has smaller angular framework  download size  there's quick detection of errors and  this also offers better security  moving on to the next question what are  components  now components are the most basic  building blocks of the ui in an angular  application  now every component is associated with a  template and is a subset of directives  only one component can be instantiated  per element in a template  now an angular application typically  consists of a root component which is  basically the app component and then it  branches out into other components  creating a hierarchy  now every component is decorated with  the help of at component decorator which  provides additional information  and component must belong to the ng  module  lastly components implement something  called the life cycle hooks you will  learn about them a little later in the  video  next up what are pipes in angular  now pipes are simple functions that are  designed to accept a particular input  value  process this value and return an output  which is a transformed value  now angular supports several built-in  pipes however you can also create custom  pipes that cater to your needs  but to speak about a few saline features  pipes are defined using the pipe symbol  pipes can be chained with other pipes  and pipes can be provided with arguments  by using the coenzyme  next up what are pure pipes  now these pipes are pipes  that use pure functions  as a result of this a pure pipe doesn't  use any internal state and the output  remains the same as long as the  parameters passed stay the same angular  calls a pure pipe only when it detects a  change in the parameters being passed  now a single instance of a pure pipe is  used throughout all components  next up what are impure pipes  now for every change detection cycle in  angular  these impure pipes are called regardless  of the change in the input fields  as long as there's a change detected  these pipes are called  as a result multiple pipe instances are  created for these pipes  now inputs passed to these pipes can  also be mutable  by default all pipes are pure however  you can also mention impure pipes using  the pure property  now here's a code for  specifying impure pipes you can use the  pure property and either mention true or  false true meaning it's a pure pipe and  false indicates that it's an impure pipe  next up what is the pipe transform  interface  now as the name suggests the interface  receives an input value  and transforms it into the desired  format with a transform method  it is typically used to implement custom  pipes  now here's again a small piece of code  now you can see that the pipe transform  interface is being used which in turn  executes the transform method now this  transform method is the one that is  responsible to change your input and  give a transformed output  moving on what is ng module  now ng modules are basically containers  that reserve a block of code to an  application domain or a workflow  now the at ng module takes a metadata  object that describes how to compile a  components template  and generate an injector at runtime  in addition to this ngmodule also  identifies the module's components  detectives services pipes and also  ensures that it makes them public so  that external components can use them  all of this is taken care of by the ng  module  next up what are filters in angular  now filters are used to format an  expression and present it to the user  they can be used in view templates  controllers or services  now to name a few  there's  date filter which formats a date to a  specified format  there's filter filter that selects a  subset of items from an array  there's the json filter which formats an  object to adjacent string  there's limit 2 which limits an array or  a string into a specified number of  elements or characters  then there's lowercase which formats a  string to lowercase  and so on moving on to the next question  what is view encapsulation in angular  now  view encapsulation basically defines  whether the template and styles defined  within the component can affect the  application or vice versa  angular provides three encapsulation  strategies  there's emulated encapsulation which  means that the styles from the main html  propagate to the component  then there is native which indicates  that the styles from the main html do  not propagated the component meaning it  does not affect the component and lastly  there's none which means that styles  from the component propagate back to the  main html and therefore are visible to  all the components on the page  now this indicates any different types  of changes and how it is affecting the  entire application  moving on what are controllers now as  the name suggests controllers control  the data of angular applications  they are regular javascript objects and  the ng controller directive defines the  application controller  next question what do you understand by  scope in angular  now the scope in angular binds the html  that is basically the view and the  javascript that is the controller it is  also an object with the available  properties and methods required for your  application  now when you make a controller in  angular you pass the dollar scope object  as an argument  moving on to the most commonly asked  question explain the life cycle hooks in  angular  as discussed earlier every component in  angular has a life cycle  angular creates and renders these  components and also destroys them before  removing them from the document object  model  it is achieved with the help of these  life cycle hooks now let's have a look  at them  first up is ng on changes now this  responds when angular sets or resets  data bound input properties  ng on it  is a hook that initializes the directive  or a component after angular first  displays the data bound properties and  sets the components input  properties ng do check detects and acts  upon the changes that angular can't or  won't detect on its own  ng after content init responds after ng  projects external content into the  components view  ng after content checked response after  angular checks the content projected  into the component  ng after viewing it responds after  angular initializes the components views  and child views  ng after view checked responds after  angular checks the components views and  the child views  lastly there's ng on destroy which  cleans up just before angular destroys  the directive or the component  moving on to the next question what is  string interpolation in angular  now string interpolation is a one-way  data binding technique that is used by  angular  now it outputs the data from typescript  code to html view  it is typically denoted with the help of  curly braces and it helps display data  from the component to the view to help  you understand it's working i've created  a variable called name  here in my  app.component.ts file and  initialized it to simplylon and back in  my html file i've created  a heading tag a header tag which  displays the name of the company is  and i've interpolated here with the help  of double curly braces  so when i run the file the output looks  something like this the name of the  company is simply learn so this is how  string interpolation is achieved in  angular moving on to next question what  are template statements  template statements are properties or  methods used in html  for responding to user events  now with these template statements the  application that you create or you're  working on can have the capability to  engage users through actions such as  submitting forms or displaying dynamic  content  most common example is the button  tag the template here is delete hero  this method is called when the user  clicks on the button  so this brings interactivity to your  application  with that we come to the end of the  first section which included the  beginner level questions  moving on let's look at some advanced  level questions  what is the difference between ahead of  time and just in time compilation  now ahead of time compilation converts  your code during the build time before  the browser downloads and runs the code  in case of just in time compilation this  process is a way of compiling computer  code to machine code during the  execution phase  aot ensures faster rendering to the  browser  while just in time is basically a  dynamic compilation  in case of ahead of time compiling  the user should include the hyphen  hyphen aot option with the ng build or  ng server command  and jit compilation is the default  compilation when you run the ng build or  ng serve cli commands  next up explain the add component  decorator  now here's a simple screenshot of what  that component decorator encompasses  is it is basically a typescript class  that is used to create  components  this genre of class is then decorated  with the add component decorator  the decorator's purpose is to accept a  metadata object that provides relevant  information about the component  now the image above shows an app  component  which is a pure typescript class  decorated with that component decorator  the object that gets accepted by the  decorator provides properties like  template url selectors style urls  and many more now here the template url  property points to an html file defining  what you see on the application  moving ahead what are services in  angular angular services  perform tasks that are used by multiple  components  now these tasks could be data fetching  network connections or database  management among others  they perform all the operational tasks  for the components and avoid rewriting  of code  a service can be written once and then  injected into all the components that  use it  generally components are used to only  display information on the ui they do  not perform any other back-end tasks  to perform tasks like validating  information or network connections etc  you can make use of a service  one advantage is that this service can  be injected into multiple components  that make use of the same piece of code  with this you can avoid redundancy  moving on what are promises and  observables  now while both the components deal with  asynchronous events in angular  promises handle one such event at a time  while observables handle a sequence of  events over some time  so to give you a brief explanation  promises emit a single value at a time  while observables are only executed when  subscribed to them using the subscribe  method  now promises also execute immediately  after they are created and they're not  cancelable  while observables help perform  operations like for each filter retry  etc promises push errors to the child  promises and observables can be  unsubscribed to so that the listener  stops receiving further values  next up what is ng on init and how is it  defined  now again here's a small snippet of code  ng on init is a life cycle hook as we  discussed earlier and there is a  callback method that is run by angular  to indicate that a component has been  created  it takes no parameters and returns a  void type  so i'm sure you can see here in the code  it takes no parameters and returns a  void  next up explain the use of ng4 in a tag  or explain the ng for directive  now the ng for directive is basically  like a for loop it is used to build  lists and tables and html templates  so in simple terms this directive is  used to iterate over an array or an  object and create template for each such  element  now in the snippet you can see there is  let items in item list and then i have  string interpolated  the  variable item so let item here creates a  local variable that will be available  inside the template  of items indicates that we are iterating  over the items iterable  and the asterisk before ng4 creates a  parent template  next up what are template and reactive  forms so there are two different methods  to create forms we have the template  driven approach and we have the reactive  form approach  so let's have a look at them  in case of template driven approach the  conventional form tag is used to create  forms angular automatically interprets  and creates a form object representation  for this tag controls can be added to  the form using the ng model tag  multiple controls can be  grouped using the ng control group  module  now a form value can be generated using  the form dot value object and form data  is exported as json values  basic html validations can be used to  validate the form fields  in the case of custom validations  directives can be used  when it comes to reactive forms  this approach basically revolves around  data flows and propagation of change  now with reactor forms the component  directly manages the data flows between  the form controls and the data models  reactive forms are code driven unlike  template-driven approach  reactive forms break the traditional  declarative approach and eliminate the  anti-pattern of updating data via the  two-way data binding method  typically reactive form control creation  is synchronous and can be unit tested  with synchronous programming techniques  moving on what is bootstrap how is it  added to angular  now bootstrap is a powerful toolkit it  is a collection of basic html css and  javascript tools for creating and  building responsive web applications  there are two ways to embed bootstrap  libraries  first up is using the bootstrap cdn  which is the content delivery network  now this enables users to load the css  and javascript files remotely from its  servers  the other way is to use angular  bootstrap via npm  now this  is used to add bootstrap to your angular  project by installing it into your  project folder  now you can use commands like npm  install bootstrap and npm install jquery  to install them for your project if you  wish to learn bootstrap in detail i  highly suggest you check out our video  on angular bootstrap the tutorial  explains how to embed bootstrap and user  to create and good looking angular  applications  what is eager and lazy loading  eager loading is the default module  loading strategy  now all the feature modules under eager  loading are loaded before your  application even starts  this is typically used for small size  applications since lesser modules are  used all of these modules are loaded  initially which makes  running of these kind of applications  extremely fast  when it comes to lazy loading  all the loading happens dynamically  all feature modules are loaded on demand  it is used for bigger applications where  the modules are not required at the  start of applications  this makes the application faster since  no time is spent on loading unnecessary  modules  next up what type of dom does angular  implement  dom or document object model  treats an xml or html document as a tree  structure  in which each node is an object  representing a part of the document  now angular uses the regular dom  this updates the entire tree structure  of html tags until it reaches the data  that has to be updated  now to ensure that the speed and  performance are not affected angular  implements something called as a change  detection  next up how is dependency injection  achieved in angular  now dependencies are objects or services  that a component needs to perform  functions correct now with the help of  dependency injection  these classes can request dependencies  from external sources rather than  creating them on their own here i've  created a service called demo service  using the command ngg service demo  service  and i've also added a small snippet of  code when you create that service  now these services can be injected to  your main component and perform various  functions  next up how does angular routing work  now i'm sure you must have observed that  the url changes every time you click on  your user interface on an application  correct every time you navigate through  the application or move from one page to  another the url changes  now this means that  the application is being routed or  you're navigating through the  application  so basically routing helps navigate  through a web application especially in  case of single page applications now as  discussed earlier single page  applications are loaded just once so any  new content that is being displayed is  just a mere addition it's not being  loaded again so routing plays a vital  role in case of single page applications  typically it is specified with the help  of the forward slash and followed by a  path that defines a new content  now i'm just taking the same example  that i took before  this was the example for string  interpolation however you can see that  we have a navigation bar here with four  different options for that is home about  services and login and for home and  login i've created  a path and added routing to it so when i  click on the home icon  you can see that  some content is being displayed onto the  screen and if you observe you can see  that there is  a forward slash with the path name home  here which indicates that routing has  occurred  same with login when i click on it the  path changes and the login page appears  if you wish to learn  the concept of routing i suggest you  check out a video the tutorial explains  routing in detail  moving on what are form control and form  groups  now a form control is basically a class  that enables validation  for each input field an instance of this  class is created  and these instances help check the  values of the field and see if they are  touched untouched dirty pristine valid  invalid and so on so for every field in  the form  the data that is being provided is  validated 